{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/214942-how-long-do-demons-keep-covers","id":214942,"title":"How long do Demons keep Covers?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-31T12:09:46-07:00","id":214942,"title":"How long do Demons keep Covers?","content":"What the title says. Also, is it common for Demons to have multiple Covers, say one for family and one for other stuff? Or do most stick with one at a time? How are players and STs handling it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-31T12:14:02-07:00","id":214962,"title":"","content":"IIRC, a cover can last until the natural end of its existence; it grows old and eventually dies. A demon certainly CAN have multiple covers, and I imagine many do, but I haven't been in a long-running game and I'll let someone else field the question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-31T13:59:06-07:00","id":215042,"title":"","content":"How long a demon keeps a Cover mostly depends on how reckless the demon is and how much they value the Cover; some weak Covers could conceivably be purchased on the cheap and burned for the purpose of a single mission, while other Covers mean the world to the demon who holds them. The only consistent effective limit is that Covers do eventually die of old age; but they don't naturally &quot;deteriorate&quot; without something happening to cause a compromise.<br /> <br /> I imagine the Unchained mostly divide into two general categories, those that keep a &quot;primary&quot; Cover they're very attached to and secondary Covers used to perform actions they'd rather not associate with the primary Cover, and those who cycle through Covers as commodities to be acquired, used, and discarded. Most demons with a single Cover are probably recently Fallen, with Primum low enough that they cannot yet sustain a second full Cover, but a lot of the demons who keep a &quot;primary&quot; Cover probably don't live out their secondary Covers very much when they're not using them for a specific purpose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T21:51:46-07:00","id":216424,"title":"","content":"The first is the preference of my players.<br /> <br /> Of course, it's boring from a narrative standpoint to have players in a place of safety, and the job of any good storyteller is to push them out of their comfort zone. If they have a cover they cherish, have the weird intrude upon it, threaten it, and make them fight to keep it.<br /> <br /> When playing ball with your son in the front yard, a black sedan with tinted windows rolls past, then slows to a crawl as they feel something press on your cover, like a finger pushing on a loose tooth. The old lady three houses down is a G-M cultist, she sacrifices a child every Halloween and erases the child from memory, <i>no Alexandra</i>, you say, <i>I won't let you go treat-or-treating</i>. The police put up security cameras in your neighborhood 'to protect the public'<br /> <br /> Dennis Detwiller has some <a href=\"http://detwillerdesign.squarespace.com/blog/2013/5/29/delta-green-creepiness-a-how-to-guide\" target=\"_blank\">appropriately sadistic</a> things to do to players. It's not intended for DtD, but you can easily adapt it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}